a. What is duck typing, as explained in the video?

Duck typing is when Python checks if an object has the needed method instead of checking what class it belongs to. Different objects can perform the same action as long as they have the required method.

b. What did the Car class need to have so it could work inside the same loop as Dog and Cat, even if it does not inherit from the Animal class?

The Car class needed to have the same method used by Dog and Cat, which is make_sound(). This allows it to work in the same loop even without inheriting from the Animal class.

class Car:
    def move(self):
        print("The car drives on the road.")


class Boat:
    def move(self):
        print("The boat sails on water.")


class Drone:
    def move(self):
        print("The drone flies in the sky.")


def start_trip(vehicle):
    vehicle.move()


car = Car()
boat = Boat()
drone = Drone()

start_trip(car)
start_trip(boat)
start_trip(drone)
